  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia Indonesia Partnership for Health Transformation (KITA SEHAT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia Indonesia Partnership for Health Transformation is an eight-year, $100 million bilateral health investment that provides catalytic support to help the Government of Indonesia (GoI) achieve its policy objectives in the intersecting fields of human and animal health, and work in key priority areas of primary care, nutrition, and stunting prevention. The program will be able to provide technical assistance, grant funding, implementation research, and institutional partnerships. It will also have a mechanism to support partnerships with Australian public sector agencies. Gender equality, disability equity and social inclusion, and climate resilience will be a strong focus of the program and will be integral for achieving national health goals.</narrative>
  </description>
